{
  "id": "irt",
  "term": "IRT",
  "definition": "IRT is an assessment approach that examines how individual test items function in relation to an underlying latent trait. Unlike test-level methods, it estimates item-level features such as difficulty and discrimination and treats measurement error as varying across levels of the trait.",
